examples.solution_text:
Centre $(2,-1)$ and radius $2$.

For the $x$-intercepts, put $y=0$:

$\begin{align*}(x-2)^{2}+1&=4\\(x-2)^{2}&=3\\x&=2\pm\sqrt{3}\end{align*}$

For the $y$-intercept, put $x=0$:

$\begin{align*}4+(y+1)^{2}&=4\\(y+1)^{2}&=0\\y&=-1\end{align*}$

The circle crosses the $x$-axis at $(2-\sqrt{3},0)$ and $(2+\sqrt{3},0)$, and touches the $y$-axis at $(0,-1)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.9cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{circleblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-0.8,0)--(5.1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-3.8)--(0,1.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,circleblue] (2,-1) circle (2);
\fill[black] (2,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2,-1) node[below right] {$(2,-1)$};
\draw[black,dashed] (2,-1)--(4,-1);
\path (3,-1) node[above] {$2$};
\fill[black] (0,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,-1) node[left] {$(0,-1)$};
\fill[black] ({2-sqrt(3)},0) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({2-sqrt(3)},0) node[above right] {$(2-\sqrt{3},0)$};
\fill[black] ({2+sqrt(3)},0) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({2+sqrt(3)},0) node[above right] {$(2+\sqrt{3},0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

